Each device must be a dictionary with exactly a unique, non-empty string `name`. Each corresponding channel list contains dictionaries with exactly non-empty string `code` and string `label`, with channel codes unique within that device. Each corresponding sample must be a dictionary whose keys are exactly those channel codes; sample values may be arbitrary objects. Malformed input, length mismatch, duplicate names/codes, or missing/extra samples raises `ValueError`.

Return device records in input order: `{'name': ..., 'channels': [{'code': ..., 'label': ..., 'value': ...}, ...]}` with channels in their input order. The complete result, including arbitrary nested sample values, must be deeply independent from every input and must contain no shared mutable nested value even if the same object appeared in multiple input sample positions. Do not mutate inputs.

